# 🤖 Face Recognition With ML And Flask App

## 🚀 Project Overview

This project implements a **Face Recognition** system deployed as a dynamic **Web Application** using the Flask micro-framework. It leverages **Machine Learning** techniques to detect, encode, and identify human faces in images or real-time video streams.

The core technology stack combines robust data processing and machine learning libraries with powerful computer vision tools to create a functional and scalable application.

---

## 🛠️ Technology Stack

| Library / Framework          | Purpose                                                                                                     |
| :--------------------------- | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Flask**                    | Micro-framework used to build the web application, handle routing, and serve HTML templates.                |
| **OpenCV** (`opencv-python`) | Core library for **Computer Vision** tasks like face detection, video stream capture, and image processing. |
| **scikit-learn**             | Used for training and implementing the classification model (e.g., K-Nearest Neighbors) on face encodings.  |
| **NumPy**                    | Fundamental library for efficient numerical operations and handling image data as multi-dimensional arrays. |
| **Pandas**                   | Utilized for data handling, managing user/face databases, and processing attendance logs (if applicable).   |
| **Matplotlib**               | Used for data visualization, debugging, and plotting analysis results (if applicable).                      |
| **Gunicorn**                 | Production-ready **WSGI HTTP Server** used to deploy the Flask application reliably.                        |
| **Pillow**                   | Image manipulation library, often used by `opencv-python` and other components for image file I/O.          |

